\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.2}{\ignorespaces Example deposition function $\delta $ applied to a sandpile with lattice size $L=4$. Numbers written at each grid cell represent the sandpile height at vertex $(x, y)$, and correspond to the cell colour. A grain is deposited at site $\mathbf  {x} = (4, 3)$, increasing the site height from 1 to 2 and producing $\eta '$.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:toy_deposition}{{1.2}{4}{Example deposition function $\delta $ applied to a sandpile with lattice size $L=4$. Numbers written at each grid cell represent the sandpile height at vertex $(x, y)$, and correspond to the cell colour. A grain is deposited at site $\mathbf {x} = (4, 3)$, increasing the site height from 1 to 2 and producing $\eta '$}{figure.caption.2}{}}
